body:
@arkology 
Hey arkology - thanks for the question! I'm a first time contributor and this is my first PR. I'm trying to come up to speed on the process you all use. Let me know what profiler tool I should use to check the editor performance. Is there some kind of results I should attache to this PR? Also if you could point me to any links that might explain more on what's expected to be tested (like performance) for a PR request that would be great.
I appreciate your help :)

@arkology 
Cool thanks for the links - I'll check them out!
Your question about the loop is good. I thought about it and I could not come up with a better way to preserve the spikes and valleys in the sampling set. I thought about trying to pre-calculate it perhaps when the frames arrived in the profiler but the sampling set is based on the zoom level so that makes it hard to pre-calculate. I'm open to suggestions from you (or anyone reading this!) on a better approach to the issue of hiding the performance spikes from the users. As you can see in the 2 videos I attached to this PR the new implementation is much more helpful to the users in finding performance spikes in their games.
